5. Arrays
map()

Transforms each element.

const nums = [1,2,3];

const doubled = nums.map(x => x * 2);

Result:

[2,4,6]
map returns new array
const nums = [1,2];

nums.map(x => x + 1);

Original remains unchanged.

filter()

Keeps matching elements.

const nums = [1,2,3,4];

const even = nums.filter(x => x % 2 === 0);

Result:

[2,4]
reduce()

Reduces array to one value.

const nums = [1,2,3,4];

const sum = nums.reduce(
    (acc, curr) => acc + curr,
    0
);

Result:

10
How reduce Works

Iteration 1:

acc = 0
curr = 1

Iteration 2:

acc = 1
curr = 2

Iteration 3:

acc = 3
curr = 3

Iteration 4:

acc = 6
curr = 4

Final:

10
Convert Array to Object
const users = [
  {id:1,name:"A"},
  {id:2,name:"B"}
];

const result = users.reduce((acc,user)=>{
   acc[user.id]=user;
   return acc;
}, {});
